<p>My hacker novel, <em>Hard Pass</em>, is in a revision draft. I need some beta readers who would be willing to check it out and give some feedback. Good or bad, it&#8217;s all helpful.</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Prerequisites</strong>: you like reading (of course) and have a strong stomach for transgressive fiction.</li>
<li><strong>Commitment level</strong>: the word count weighs in at approximately 50K (the length of <em>The Great Gatsby</em>, about a 4-5 hour read if you&#8217;re speedy).</li>
</ul>
<p>Here&#8217;s the plot: <strong>A hacker gets a job as an IT technician for a low-tier Florida university and immediately he&#8217;s drafted as a digital mercenary helping coeds get their photos removed from a notorious revenge-porn site. But the true test comes when the girl he loves asks him to help fix her boyfriend&#8217;s grades. Will our anti-hero risk jail time for a woman who&#8217;ll never be his?</strong></p>
<p>There&#8217;s only one way to find out. You can contact me directly through the form below to let me know you&#8217;re interested.</p>
<p>For those who care about such things, no part of the manuscript was generated with AI tooling. As wacky as the plot sounds it&#8217;s <strong>100% human-grade lunacy</strong>.</p>
<p>Your input will help turn this leaky bark into a streamlined dirigible.</p>
